**Issue**: #357
**Date**: 2026-09-03
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG
**Related Spec**: specs/284-resolve-missing-required-check-event-provenance/

@issue-357 @bug @delivery @check-provenance
Feature: Canonicalize explicit pull_request_target delivery checks
  Delivery previously preserved an explicit pull_request_target event even when
  its linked Actions run matched the exact PR head, causing valid snapshots to fail.
  Exact-head target events are now canonicalized without dropping the check.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Explicit exact-head target event is canonicalized
    Given a successful observed PR check explicitly reports event "pull_request_target"
    And its linked Actions run head SHA equals the PR head
    When delivery builds and classifies the exact-head snapshot
    Then the check remains in the snapshot with event "pull_request"
    And the check does not by itself make delivery evidence invalid

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Unsafe explicit provenance remains rejected
    Given a successful observed check has <condition>
    When delivery builds and classifies the exact-head snapshot
    Then the check is not canonicalized to event "pull_request"
    And the check cannot make the snapshot merge-ready

    Examples:
      | condition                                      |
      | event "push"                                  |
      | event "merge_group"                           |
      | an empty event with no resolvable Actions run  |
      | a pull_request_target run at a different head  |
      | an unreadable pull_request_target Actions run  |
      | another non-PR event                           |
